invariant: INV-16
file: srv_auth.c
catches: quic_loop_host
reason: the server signs its CertificateVerify with its P-256 key under
  WIDEMUL_NOT_STATED whatever its ch_cfg.cpu states: it hands
  p256_sign_hedged_cpu the value without CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY.
  The signature still verifies. test/quic_loop_widemul.h runs the r2
  identity, a P-256 key, and requires a server whose ch_cfg.cpu holds
  CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY to call no file under its own names.

--- old
    int signed_ok = p256_sign_hedged_cpu(cfg->cpu, id->priv, digest, noise, sig, cap, sig_len);
--- new
    int signed_ok = p256_sign_hedged_cpu(cfg->cpu & ~(uint32_t)CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY,
                                         id->priv, digest, noise, sig, cap, sig_len);
